# Opt63 (2026-10-30): STRATA_KVT_LAZY=<N> (inert unless set; config D sets 0): when the elastic K/V is trimmed at the start of a request (a long prompt earlier left it
# grown), only the first N of the freed slots are refilled before the request; the rest join the D18 pending refill (idle time and decode pieces), the same path the
# prompt loan's slots already take. Measured (128K needle in conversation A, then 94-token requests of conversation B, x2): first request after the trim 11.6 s -> 4.5 s
# prompt time (N=0; 300: 7.2 s), its decode -4 %, the next request's -7 % until the idle fill (7.6-10 s); 0 GPU timeouts. Quality gate vs p-off PASS alone (p99 0.0955,
